{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for persistent upward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 3-5 EUR in the short term (days 1-5) and 8-12 EUR in the medium term (days 10-20) during downtrends, regardless of sentiment.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion after price spikes: When history shows a spike (e.g., >85 EUR) followed by a drop, the model fails to anticipate the depth of the correction; reduce forecasts by 2-4 EUR immediately following such peaks.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: Positive sentiment scores (1.00) do not trigger immediate price increases in the model; if sentiment is high but the last 3 days show declining prices, lower the forecast by 1.5-2.5 EUR to reflect the lagged market reaction.",
    "Extend the downtrend horizon: The model assumes a floor around 82-83 EUR; when the trend is clearly bearish (history declining for >5 days), extend the downward trajectory by 2-3 EUR beyond the model's predicted bottom.",
    "Ignore flat sentiment in volatile regimes: When sentiment oscillates between 0.00 and 0.67 while prices are falling, the model's flat or slightly rising forecast is invalid; force a downward slope of 0.5-1.0 EUR per day."
  ]
}
